swi_a = True
swi_b = True
swi_c = True
swi_d = True

### <devA>-<devB> = <portOnA>-<portOnB>, comma-separated. The literal device "tb" =
### the testbox itself. Each declared link is CONSUMED by one init_portlink() call,
### so two calls between the same pair need two links declared here.
###
### A portlink names the MEMBER switch, never the stack: Setup.py keys links on the
### member and `get_temporary_testbox_portlink()` walks the other stack members
### itself when the queried member has no direct link.
###
### VERIFIED 2026-08-31 by MAC cross-match from BOTH ends (LLDP is off across this
### bench, so the method is `show mac address-table` against known NIC/base MACs):
###   swi_b port1.0.1 <-> swi_d port1.0.1
###       swi_d port1.0.1 has learnt 0000.cd37.0d6f -- the IE520 STACK virtual MAC --
###       and it is the only swi_d port that has. Both ends read connected,
###       a-full / a-1000. Media differs and that is fine: 10GBASE-T pluggable on the
###       IE520 against 1000BASE-T on the x230, negotiating 1 G.
###
### CONNECTED BUT FAR END NOT POSITIVELY IDENTIFIED -- deliberately NOT declared,
### because a guessed portlink is hardware-specific fabrication:
###   swi_a port2.0.1  (10GBASE-TM) connected, a-full/a-1000, has learnt NO MACs
###   swi_a port2.0.9  (1000BASE-T) connected, a-full/a-1000, has learnt NO MACs
###   Most likely the DIRECT IE520<->AR4050S pair that, together with the path via
###   the x230, forms the L2 loop the 2026-08-26 handover §3 warns about (measured
###   previously at 86.7 % loss / 2.6 s RTT, cured by shutting po1). The AR4050S has
###   four ports up (port1.0.1-1.0.4) and has learnt the IE520 stack MAC on
###   port1.0.3 -- i.e. via the x230, not on a direct port -- so the direct pair
###   carries no traffic today and cannot be pinned by MAC learning alone.
###   To resolve: shut one AR4050S port at a time and watch which IE520 port drops.
###   That is a MUTATING check on a live bench and needs sign-off first.
###
### NOT PRESENT, contrary to the previous version of this file:
###   tb-swi_a = eth3-port1.0.23 is GONE. port1.0.23 does not exist on swi_a (swi_a
###   is member 2); the member-1 port1.0.23 reads notconnect with NO pluggable
